      "source_prose_extracts": [
        "Zulrah is a level 725 solo-only snake boss . Before the player can fight Zulrah, players must have completed Regicide to the point of reaching Port Tyras , as well as having spoken with High Priestess Zul-Harcinqa to offer themselves as the sacrifice in place of the gnome child , as Zul-Gwenwynig will prevent the player from boarding the boat until Zul-Harcinqa allows them to be the sacrifice.",
        "When a player defeats Zulrah, the drops will be received under the player, much like cave krakens . A Zul-andra teleport scroll will also be dropped near the player, which cannot be picked up but can be used to return to Zul-Andra. To fight Zulrah again after, the player must return to the shrine via the boat.",
        "In addition to the 100% drops, the player will also have two rolls on Zulrah's drop table, excluding tertiary items, which have only one roll. The displayed drop chances represent a single roll.",
        "There is a 1/128 chance of hitting the unique drop table per kill. [ 4 ] Zulrah gives two rolls per kill, meaning there's approximately a 1/512 chance per kill to receive a specific item from this table (or ~1/128 for any item). Below lists the approximate drop rates per roll of any specific item, which takes into account the fact that there are 4 different items in this drop table. Although uncut onyx appears on the unique drop table and in the collection log, it is not exclusive to Zulrah.",
        "There is a 10/249 chance to roll on the flax table, followed by a 10/2,632 chance to roll on the mutagen sub-table. [ 5 ] Each mutagen is equally likely, making the drop rate per kill approximately 1/6,554 for a specific mutagen or 1/3,277 for either mutagen."
      ],
